The adapter-neutral helper preserves outputs via the VFS atomic publication
contract. It does not implement Native interactive stdin,complete stderr logs,
or empty native OS files after failed mux header initialization. Canonical
Node/workerd fixtures cover13named single-output profiles and MP4 copy;other
paths still require separate sequencing/protocol verification.

Default complex/replay graphs and explicit timed command schedulers share this
preflight before allocating output/spool state. All outputs are checked before
opening any writer;this retains Edge atomic publication rather than Native
sequential OS opening side effects. Explicit negative status propagation through
ComplexVideoFailure only applies when its cleanup succeeds.
